  "name": "Salt Songs (Southern Paiute and Chemehuevi mourning cycle)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "A long cycle of songs of the Southern Paiute and Chemehuevi that traces a journey, the Salt Song Trail, through sacred places of their homelands in present-day Nevada, Utah, Arizona and California, sung through the night at funerals and memorial gatherings to accompany the spirit of the dead. Singers accompany themselves with gourd rattles. The Salt Song Project brought singers from many bands together to revive the cycle, as documented in the film The Salt Song Trail: Bringing Creation Back Together (2005). The shaker card stands in for the gourd rattle.",
